<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tobruk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tobruk is a port city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> its harbour made it a key objective in the North African campaign: an Allied garrison, largely the Australian 9th Division, held it against German and Italian forces under Rommel through the siege of 1941, later joined by British, Polish and Czechoslovak troops. It fell to Rommel in June 1942.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tobruk.jpg" alt="Tobruk" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Mario1952 at Italian Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tobruk_port.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
